---

## ⚙️ Part 1 & 2: Model Discovery and Comparison

### 📊 Dataset
- Source: UCI Adult Income Dataset
- Rows: 32,561
- Target Variable: `income` (<=50K or >50K)

---

### 🤖 PyCaret Workflow
Using PyCaret, models were automatically trained and compared using cross-validation.

**Top 3 Models:**
1. Light Gradient Boosting Machine (LGBMClassifier)
2. Gradient Boosting Classifier
3. AdaBoost Classifier

LightGBM achieved the highest accuracy (~87%).

---

### 🧠 Scikit-learn Workflow
The best model family (LightGBM) was manually rebuilt using:
- train-test split (80/20)
- preprocessing pipeline:
  - numerical: imputation + scaling
  - categorical: imputation + one-hot encoding

**Classification Report Summary:**
- Accuracy: ~87%
- Strong performance on <=50K class
- Slightly lower recall for >50K class

---

## 📊 Confusion Matrix

The confusion matrix below shows model performance:

- True Negatives (<=50K correctly predicted): 4639
- False Positives: 306
- False Negatives: 514
- True Positives (>50K correctly predicted): 1054

This indicates strong overall performance, with some difficulty identifying high-income individuals.

> 📌 See: `Confusion Matrix.png`

---

## 🚀 Part 3: Model Deployment (FastAPI)

A FastAPI application was built to serve predictions.

### ▶️ Run the API

```bash
uvicorn main:app --reload

Then open: http://127.0.0.1:8000/docs

Sample input you can use to predict:
{
  "age": 39,
  "workclass": "State-gov",
  "fnlwgt": 77516,
  "education": "Bachelors",
  "education_num": 13,
  "marital_status": "Never-married",
  "occupation": "Adm-clerical",
  "relationship": "Not-in-family",
  "race": "White",
  "sex": "Male",
  "capital_gain": 2174,
  "capital_loss": 0,
  "hours_per_week": 40,
  "native_country": "United-States"
}

And the sample output should look like:
{
  "prediction": "<=50K"
}

🧠 Conclusion
This project demonstrates how low-code tools and traditional machine learning workflows complement each other. PyCaret is ideal for rapid experimentation, while scikit-learn offers more control for production environments. Deploying the model with FastAPI enables real-time predictions, completing the full ML pipeline.